(:id "port/python/vt/fixed-class" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/vtfixedclass_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtFixedClassRows, TestPythonVtFixedClassRowsNegativeControl" "make python-vt-fixed-class-rows python-vt-fixed-class-rows-negative-control (make/python-vt-fixed-class-rows.mk, make/negative-controls.d/python-vt-fixed-class-rows-negative-control.json)") :tested-revision "5cac2d50ca9ab4546b5ea4d84a13bc6930b279a7" :note "2026-11-17: the fixed-class row's manifest corpus (the tabledemo roots, the V1/V2 evolution seams, the P1 chain, the form-byte refusals and a previous-form wide blob) reads through the generated fixed reader and saves back byte-identical with measure equal to the file's length, or refuses as the manifest says; a report row answers reports.txt's verdict. Both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2, make dist-python) run every case and agree. The negative control moves the fixed file's last header byte in a copy of the emitted runtime and every accepted instance row goes red by its own name. The kind runtime was already green at the base, so no kind module changed and no bench numbers move. Run on Linux x86-64, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
(:id "port/python/vt/build-version" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/vtfixedclass_test.go: TestPythonVtFixedClassBuildVersion, TestPythonVtFixedClassBuildVersionImports, TestPythonVtFixedClassBuildVersionImportsNegativeControl" "make python-vt-fixed-class-negative-control (make/python-vt-fixed-class.mk)") :tested-revision "5cac2d50ca9ab4546b5ea4d84a13bc6930b279a7" :note "2026-11-17: every table corpus unit's generated package carries BUILD_VERSION as a literal beside PROTOCOL_ID and it equals the engine's build version, held by TestPythonVtFixedClassBuildVersion; TestPythonVtFixedClassBuildVersionImports imports each generated package under both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2, make dist-python) and checks the exported constant, after mypy --strict over the package. The negative control moves the emitted constant in a copy and the import check goes red by name under both pins. Run on Linux x86-64, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
